         "Split into ES modules and set up for npm"
Files:   gml.js gml-player.js gml-ui.js gml-ui.css, byte for byte from
         that commit. Public domain, no rights reserved.

Why here and not app/assets: Propshaft fingerprints filenames, which
breaks the modules' relative imports (`import ... from './gml.js'`).
Thruster serves public/ in production.

To update:
  1. In a clean canvasplayer checkout, `node --test test.js`.
  2. Copy the four files into public/canvasplayer/<new version>/ and
     write a new SOURCE there with the commit.
  3. Bump the version in ApplicationHelper#canvasplayer_path.
  4. `bundle exec rspec spec/requests/canvasplayer_spec.rb`, then open
     a tag page. Delete the old version directory.

Edits belong upstream first. Anything that had to land here instead is
listed below, so it can be carried back.

